## Part 1: Syntax Errors
```java
public class SyntaxPractice {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Learning Java");
        System.out.println("Finding errors is an important skill");
    }
}


### Questions:
1) Two errors: a missing semicolon after the first println, and a missing closing quotation mark plus missing semicolon on the second println.
2) The first line was missing its semicolon at the end.
3) The second line's string literal was never closed with a final double quote.
4) No, the compiler often flags the error on the line after the actual mistake, since it doesn't realize a statement is incomplete until it reads the next line.

